WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:06.930
Back in New York, Mr. Hobbs was still missing Cedric.

2
00:00:06.931 --> 00:00:11.942
It was the end of the day, and the grocer was sitting alone in his store.

3
00:00:11.943 --> 00:00:16.435
"No one can take Cedric's place," Mr. Hobbs thought.

4
00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:20.458
"But it would be good to talk to someone besides myself.

5
00:00:20.459 --> 00:00:25.146
Cedric was always mentioning another friend of his—Dick.

6
00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:30.990
Maybe Dick's looking for a new friend too."

7
00:00:30.991 --> 00:00:35.852
The next day Mr. Hobbs went for a shoeshine at Dick's stand.

8
00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:41.107
He wasn't quite sure how to start the conversation.

9
00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:45.428
"This is a nice stand," Mr. Hobbs finally said.

10
00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:48.967
"A friend of mine set me up in business."

11
00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:53.715
Dick applied some polish to Mr. Hobbs' shoes.

12
00:00:53.716 --> 00:00:56.322
"He was the best little guy you ever met.

13
00:00:56.323 --> 00:01:01.497
He's in England now, learning to be an earl."

14
00:01:01.498 --> 00:01:04.733
"Would that be Lord Fauntleroy?"

15
00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:09.106
Dick was so surprised that he dropped his cloth.

16
00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:13.209
"Yes! Do you know Cedric too?"

17
00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:20.712
"I've known him since he was born. I'm Mr. Hobbs, the grocer."

18
00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.931
Dick shook Mr. Hobbs' hand enthusiastically.

19
00:01:24.932 --> 00:01:28.099
"Cedric told me all about you!"

20
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:34.645
Mr. Hobbs grinned. "And I feel like I already know you."

21
00:01:34.646 --> 00:01:43.699
"I miss Cedric." Dick picked up his cloth and went back to polishing Mr. Hobbs' shoes. "Whenever

22
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.524
I was feeling down, he always cheered me up." "Me

23
00:01:47.525 --> 00:01:53.116
too." Mr. Hobbs nodded in agreement. Cedric's

24
00:01:53.117 --> 00:02:00.406
friends soon realized they had a lot to discuss. Mr.

25
00:02:00.407 --> 00:02:05.260
Hobbs invited Dick to visit him the next evening. After

26
00:02:05.261 --> 00:02:11.120
that the two quickly became friends. They

27
00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:16.963
enjoyed reading Cedric's letters aloud and writing to him. Dick

28
00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:21.731
often needed help writing letters. One

29
00:02:21.732 --> 00:02:27.212
night he looked over Mr. Hobbs' shoulder while the grocer edited his letter. "I

30
00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.904
didn't have much schooling because I was always working. I

31
00:02:30.905 --> 00:02:36.025
got a job as soon as I was old enough to sell newspapers and run errands." Mr.

32
00:02:36.026 --> 00:02:39.539
Hobbs handed Dick's letter back to him. "Why

33
00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.532
did you start working so young?" "After

34
00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:47.211
my parents died, my brother, Ben, took care of me. He

35
00:02:47.212 --> 00:02:51.035
had a job in a store, but we both needed to make money. Everything

36
00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:54.913
was fine until he married Minna." Dick

37
00:02:54.914 --> 00:03:01.534
rolled his eyes. "I guess he liked her because she was pretty with long, dark hair. But

38
00:03:01.535 --> 00:03:05.098
she had such a terrible temper!" After

39
00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:10.913
Minna had a baby, she sometimes made Dick take care of him. "When

40
00:03:10.914 --> 00:03:16.106
baby Tom cried, Minna would throw things at me !" Dick said.

41
00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:19.591
"Like it was my fault that her baby was screaming!"

42
00:03:19.592 --> 00:03:24.145
"She sounds dreadful," Mr. Hobbs said.

43
00:03:24.146 --> 00:03:28.067
"Once she threw a plate at me and hit the baby instead!

44
00:03:28.068 --> 00:03:31.393
The plate cut Tom's chin."

45
00:03:31.394 --> 00:03:35.977
Dick shook his head as if he still couldn't believe the story.

46
00:03:35.978 --> 00:03:39.399
"The doctor said Tom would always have that scar."

47
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.397
"I hope you don't live with them now."

48
00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:47.268
"Oh, no. Minna was angry that Ben wasn't making enough money.

49
00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:50.289
So he went out west to work on a ranch.

50
00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.999
A week later Minna and Tom left.

51
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.159
Ben and I never heard from them again."

52
00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:04.978
*** Soon after the earl's dinner party, Mr. Hobbs had an important letter to show

53
00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:11.785
Dick. "Cedric's no longer Lord Fauntleroy!" the grocer announced as soon as Dick entered the

54
00:04:11.786 --> 00:04:17.049
store. "I don't believe it!" Dick sat on Cedric's old

55
00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:21.138
stool. Mr. Hobbs began to read Cedric's letter

56
00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:22.980
aloud. Dear Mr.

57
00:04:22.981 --> 00:04:28.902
Hobbs, I have some surprising news for you. There has been a

58
00:04:28.903 --> 00:04:34.530
mistake. I am not a lord, and I won't be an earl when my grandfather

59
00:04:34.531 --> 00:04:38.728
dies. A woman is saying that she was married to my uncle Bevis.

60
00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:45.580
This means their son is Lord Fauntleroy, because Bevis was the earl's older son.

61
00:04:45.581 --> 00:04:50.687
At first I worried I'd have to give this boy my pony and cart.

62
00:04:50.688 --> 00:04:56.127
But Grandpapa says I may keep them. (I don't think he likes this woman.)

63
00:04:56.128 --> 00:05:01.696
Grandpapa probably thinks Mama and I are happy I won't be an earl.

64
00:05:01.697 --> 00:05:09.215
But I've grown to like the idea. You can do so much for people when you're rich.

65
00:05:09.216 --> 00:05:17.353
Sadly, I'm not rich anymore. I'll have to get a job so I can take care of Mama.

66
00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:22.509
I'm going to ask the head groom about becoming a groom or a coachman.

67
00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.799
Your friend,

68
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:29.059
Cedric Errol (not Lord Fauntleroy)

69
00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.472
"They're trying to cheat Cedric out of his title because he's an American!"

70
00:05:33.473 --> 00:05:39.135
Mr. Hobbs pounded his fist on a barrel. "We have to help him."

71
00:05:39.136 --> 00:05:41.850
"Of course we do!" Dick said.

72
00:05:41.851 --> 00:05:45.415
"He can be my partner in the shoeshine business."

73
00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:51.388
"And I'll offer him a partnership in the grocery store," Mr. Hobbs said.

74
00:05:51.389 --> 00:05:58.551
The friends discussed the situation over a supper of biscuits, cheese, and sardines.

75
00:05:58.552 --> 00:06:04.422
Then they wrote Cedric a letter together.

